id.instance: String (TS "c<n>")
num.game: i32
num.cursor: u32
map.ordered: IndexMap
bag.data: IndexMap<String, serde_json::Value>
error.style: Result<_, EngineError> with TS's message; panic only on invariants (every TS `why*`/refusal `string | null` is Result<(), EngineError>, Ok for null)
null.optional: Option + skip_serializing_if
null.nullable: Option, serialised null
case.json: camelCase via serde rename_all
case.rust: snake_case
state.mut: &mut GameState writes, &GameState reads, &mut EngineSink for TS sink mutators
rng.source: Rng::new(&state.seed, state.rng_cursor) and write the cursor back
hook.style: Arc<dyn Fn + Send + Sync> via hook(); no fn pointers, no Box
registry.style: OnceLock set once by register_all; fused scripts built on lookup from state
async.style: tokio in crates/server only; none in pure crates
log.style: tracing JSON to stdout, server only
script.lookup: scripts::script_of(&GameState, def_id) -> CardScripts (SURFACE §6.6); TS scriptOf(instance) is a private script_of_card(state, card) in each file (Vanilla → empty_script(), radiant → .radiant)
instance.moved: a TS function that moves or writes the instance it is handed takes &mut CardInstance; one handed a card already out of its pile takes it by value (draw::complete_draw); later writes go through state::find_instance_mut
zones.reads: card_at -> Option<&CardInstance>, active_units_of -> Vec<&CardInstance>, ZoneSlot passed as &ZoneSlot
optional.args: TS default/optional params are Option (None = TS default); list defaults are &[T] (callers pass &[]); options-object args are passed Default::default()
